          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em vielbein
            or
            %em solder form
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a linear identification of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            with explicit (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-orthogonal+structure"}> pseudo-
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"}> orthogonal structure
            \.
          %p
            Any such choice encodes a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"}> pseudo-
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p There are different equivalent perspectives on the notion of vielbein that are closely related:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#InTermsOfCartanGeometry"} In terms of Cartan geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#InTermsOfOrthogonalStructure"} In terms of orthogonal structure
          %h3#InTermsOfCartanGeometry In terms of Cartan geometry
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+1-form"} Lie algebra valued 1-form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔦𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (E,\Omega) : T X \to \mathfrak{iso}(d)
          %p
            with values in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
            encodes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"} pseudo-Riemannian metric
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (if non-degenerate, at least). In this context the component
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E : T X \to \mathbb{R}^d
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            1-form is called the
            %em vielbein
            \. It encodes the metric by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Sym
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g = \langle E \otimes E\rangle  \in Sym^2_{C^\infty(X)} \Gamma(T^* X)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle : \mathbb{R}^d \times \mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R}
            is the canonical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
          %p
            In other words, Given an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ISO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (SO(d) \hookrightarrow ISO(d))
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+connection"} Cartan connection
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em vielbein
            is the isomorphism in the definition of Cartan connection.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d=4
            this is the
            %em vierbein
            , for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 3
            the
            %em dreibein
            , etc.
          %p
            This terminology is used notably in the context of the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+formulation+of+gravity"} first-order formulation of gravity
          %h3#InTermsOfOrthogonalStructure In terms of orthogonal structure
          %p
            We discuss here how a choice of vielbein on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+structure+groups"} reduction of the structure group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            to its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+compact+subgroup"} maximal compact subgroup
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
          %p
            The following also introduces the description of this in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+vielbein"} generalized vielbein
            fields and generally to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+c-structures"} twisted differential c-structures
          %h4#ClassOfTheTangentBundle The class of the tangent bundle
          %p
            For completeness, we first review how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            is naturally incarnated as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
            and how this in turn is naturally formulated in terms of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} smooth
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ReductionOfTheStructureGroup"} next section
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            By definition this means that there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi i
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\phi_i^{-1} : \mathbb{R}^n \simeq U_i \hookrightarrow X\}
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+charts"} coordinate charts
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \cap U_j
            of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+charts"} coordinate charts
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivatives"} partial derivatives
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+transformations"} coordinate transformations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi j
                  %mo ∘
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi i
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi_j\circ \phi_i^{-1}
                  \:
                  U_i \cap U_j \subset \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^n
          %p
            form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobian+matrix"} Jacobian matrix
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi μ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mfrac
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi ν
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi j
                    %mo ∘
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ]
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ((\lambda_{i j})^{\mu}{}_{\nu})
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\left[\frac{d}{d x^\nu} \phi_j \circ \phi_i^{-1} (x^\mu)
                  \\right]
                  \:
                  U_i \cap U_j
                  \\to
                  GL_n
          %p
            with values in invertible
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrices"} matrices
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+rule"} chain rule
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+product"} matrix product
            equations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi μ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi λ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi μ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\lambda_{i j})^\mu{}_\lambda (\lambda_{j k})^\lambda{}_{\nu}
                  \=
                  (\lambda_{i k})^\mu{}_{\nu}
                  \\,,
          %p hence the equation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\lambda_{i j} \cdot \lambda_{j k} = \lambda_{i k}
          %p
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(U_i \cap U_j, GL(n))
            of smooth
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            condition for a smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cocycle
            in degree 1 with coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            (precisely: with coefficients in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of smooth functions with values in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            ):
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi smooth
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [(\lambda_{i j})] \in H^1_{smooth}(X, GL_n)
                  \\,.
          %p
            It is useful to formulate this statement in the language of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stacks"} differentiable stacks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                itself is trivially a Lie groupoid
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \stackrel{\to}{\to} X)
            %li
              %p
                from the atlas
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
                we get the corresponding
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+groupoid"} Cech groupoid
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi j
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      C(\{U_i\}) =
                      (\coprod_{i, j} U_i \cap U_j \stackrel{\to}{\to} \coprod_i U_i)
            %li
              %p
                any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                induces its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi G
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo →
                        %mo *
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbf{B}G
                      \=
                      \\left(
                      G \stackrel{\to}{\to} *
                      \\right)
                      \\,.
          %p
            The above situation is neatly encoded in the existence of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            of Lie groupoids of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi λ
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo .
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mo ≃
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  C(\{U_i\}) &amp;\stackrel{\lambda}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B} GL(n).
                  \\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{\simeq}}\downarrow
                  \\\
                  X
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the left morphism is
                = succeed "-wise" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhoods"} neighbourhoods
                of each point) an
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
            %li
              %p
                the horizontal functor has as components the functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{i j}
                and its functoriality is the cocycle condition
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{i j} \cdot \lambda_{j k} = \lambda_{i k}
          %p
            We want to think of such a diagram as being directly a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth groupoids
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  T X : X \to \mathbf{B} GL(n) \;\; \in \mathbf{H}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is true in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            in which stalkwise equivalences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi SmthMfd
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \subset Mor(PSh(SmthMfd, Grpd))
            have been
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} formally inverted
            to become
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
          %p
            Since all real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are encoded by such morphisms, as are their
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} GL(n)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            for real vector bundles.
          %p Of course there is a “smaller” Lie groupoid that also classifies real vector bundles. Passing to this “smaller” Lie groupoid is what the choice of vielbein accomplishes, to which we now turn.
          %h4#ReductionOfTheStructureGroup Reduction of the structure group
          %p
            Consider the defining inclusion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  O(n) \hookrightarrow GL(n)
                  \\,.
          %p
            We may understand this inclusion geometrically in terms of the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric"} metric
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+compact+subgroup"} maximal compact subgroup
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            (it is a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            %em only
            encodes geometric information.
          %p The inclusion induces a corresponding morphism of moduli stacks
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{c} : \mathbf{B} O(n) \to \mathbf{B} GL(n)
                  \\,.
          %p
            A choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = O(n)
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi h
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi λ
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi E
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi c
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X &amp;&amp;\stackrel{h}{\to}&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B} O(n)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\lambda}}\searrow &amp;\swArrow_{E^{-1}}&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\mathbf{c}}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}GL(n)
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p This consists of two pieces of data
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
                is a
                = succeed "-valued" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
                %em orthogonal transition functions
                – hence on each overlap of coordinate patches a smooth function
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                        %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      ((h_{i j}){}^a{}_b) : U_i \cap U_j \to O(n)
              %p such that
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ;
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      h_{i j} \cdot h_{j k} = h_{i k}
                      \\,;
            %li
              %p
                the homotopy
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                is on each chart a function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_i  = ((E_i)^a{}_\mu) : U_i \to GL(n)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                such that on each double overlap it intertwines the transition functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                of the tangent bundle with the new orthogonal transition functions, meaning that the equation
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi i
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                        %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi μ
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                        %mi ν
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                        %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi j
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi b
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                        %mi ν
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (E_i)^a{}_{\mu} (\lambda_{i j})^{\mu}{}_\nu
                      \=
                      (h_{i j})^a{}_b (E_j]^b{}_\nu
              %p
                holds. This exhibits the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                of
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi E
                                    %mi i
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi h
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi i
                                        %mi j
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi λ
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi i
                                        %mi j
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi E
                                    %mi j
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      * &amp;\stackrel{E_i}{\to}&amp; *
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{h_{i j}}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\lambda_{i j}}}
                      \\\
                      * &amp;\stackrel{E_j}{\to}&amp; *
                      }
          %p
            Such a lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (h,E)
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is called the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %strong vielbein
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E : T X \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} V
          %p
            between a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to X
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
            explicitly being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+structure+groups"} reduction of the structure group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
          %h4#ModuliSpaceOfOrhtogonalStructures Moduli space of orthogonal structures: twisted cohomology
          %p
            In order to understand the space of choices of vielbein fields on a given tangent bundle, hence the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structures"} orthogonal structures
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metrics"} Riemannian metrics
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of the morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c} : \mathbf{B}O(n) \to \mathbf{B}GL(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset"} coset
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo \
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n) \backslash GL(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  GL(n)/O(n) &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B} O(n)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B} GL(n)
                  }
          %p
            as being a bundle in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}GL(n)
            with typical fiber
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)/O(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+infinity-bundle"} associated bundle
            to the smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal GL(n)-bundle
            induced by the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo \
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)\backslash GL(n)
          %p
            This means that if the tangent bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            is trivializable, then the coset space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo \
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)\backslash GL(n)
            is the moduli space for vielbein fields on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo \
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo \
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}(X, O(n)\backslash GL(n)) = C^\infty(X, O(n)\backslash GL(n))
                  \\,.
          %p
            However, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            is not trivial, then this is true only locally: there is then an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
            such that restricted to each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            the moduli space of vielbein fields is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(U_i, GL(n)/ O(n))
          %p
            the tangent bundle
            %em twists
            the functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to GL(n)/O(n)
            = succeed "-_" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            = succeed "_" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            %em twisting coefficient bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
          %p We can make this more manifest by writing equivalently
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo \
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo \
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  O(n)\backslash GL(n) &amp;\to&amp; (O(n)\backslash GL(n)) // GL(n)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}GL(n)
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            where now on the right we have inserted the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            resolution of the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
            as provided by the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            of the action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo \
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)\backslash GL(n)
          %p The pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mrow
                              %mi GL
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo \
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo \
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi T
                              %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  T X \times_{GL(n)} (O(n)\backslash GL(n))
                  \&amp;\to&amp;
                  O(n)\backslash GL(n) // GL(n)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{T X}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}GL(n)
                  }
          %p
            give the non-linear
            = succeed "-associated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            = succeed "-0-cohomology\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo \
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)\backslash GL(n)
          %h4#moduli_stack_of_orthogonal_structures Moduli stack of orthogonal structures
          %p
            The above says that the space of vielbein fields is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over-%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} slice (2,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}GL(n)}
            with coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c} : \mathbf{B}O \to \mathbf{B}GL(n)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %msub
                    %mi Struc
                    %mi TX
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  O Struc_{TX}(X) \simeq \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}GL(n)}(T X, \mathbf{c})
                  \\,.
          %p
            But also this space of choices of vielbein fields has a smooth structure, it is itself a smooth
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            in the slice over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}GL(n)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} locally cartesian closed (2,1)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Struc
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  O \mathbf{Struc}_{T X}(X)
                  \=
                  [X, \mathbf{B}O]_{\mathbf{B}GL(n)}
          %h4#differential_refinement_spin_connection Differential refinement: Spin connection
          %p
            We may further lift this discussion to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            to get genuine
            %em differential
            = succeed "-twisted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            = succeed "-structures." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie-algebra+valued+forms"} groupoid of Lie-algebra valued forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} SmoothGrpd
            this the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connections
          %p
            The morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
            has an evident differential refinement
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mi conn
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{c}_{conn} : \mathbf{B}O(n)_{conn} \to \mathbf{B}GL(n)_{conn}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of this differential refinement is still the same as before
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  GL(n)/ O(n) &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B} O(n)_{conn}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B} GL(n)_{conn}
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p so that the moduli space of “differential vielbein fields” is the same as that of plain vielbein fields.
          %p
            Consider an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+connection"} affine connection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\nabla_{T X} : X \to \mathbf{B}GL(n)
          %p
            hence a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            which locally on out atas is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoffel+symbols"} Christoffel symbols
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi μ
                  %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔤𝔩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Gamma_i = ((\Gamma_i)_\mu{}{}^{\alpha}{}_\beta)
                  \\in
                  \\Omega^1(U_i, \mathfrak{gl}(n))
                  \\,.
          %p
            A lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\nabla_V, E)
            in
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo ∇
                                %mi V
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi O
                            %mi conn
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ∇
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi T
                                    %mi X
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi E
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi c
                                %mi conn
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\nabla_{V}}{\to}&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}O_{conn}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\nabla_{T X}}}\searrow
                  \&amp;\swArrow_{E^{-1}}&amp;
                  \\swarrow_{\mathbf{c}_{conn}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}GL(n)_{conn}
                  }
          %p
            is in components a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+connection"}> spin connection
            ”
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi μ
                  %mo =
                  %mi E
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi μ
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega_\mu = E d E^{-1} + E \Gamma_\mu E^{-1}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi μ
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi μ
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi ν
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi μ
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi λ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega_\mu{}^a{}_b
                  \=
                  E^a{}_\nu \partial_\mu E^\nu{}_b
                  +
                  E^a{}_\nu \Gamma_\mu{}^\nu{}_\lambda E^\lambda{}_b
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the standard formula for the relation between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoffel+symbols"} Christoffel symbols
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+connection"} spin connection
            in terms of the vielbein.
          %h4#generalized_and_exceptional_vielbein_fields Generalized and exceptional vielbein fields
          %p The above discussion seamlessly generalizes to many other related cases. For instance
          %ol
            %li
              %p For the coefficient bundle
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi O
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo \
                              %mi O
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi O
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi O
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ×
                              %mi O
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi O
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      O(n)\backslash O(n,n) /O(n) &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B} (O(n) \times O(n))
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}O(n,n)
                      }
              %p
                one gets the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+vielbein"} generalized vielbein
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+geometry"} type II geometry
            %li
              %p for the coefficient bundle
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi H
                                %mi n
                              %mo \
                              %msub
                                %mi E
                                %mi n
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %msub
                                %mi H
                                %mi n
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %msub
                                %mi E
                                %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      H_n\backslash E_n &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B} H_n
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B} E_n
                      }
              %p
                coming from the inclusion of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+compact+subgroup"} maximal compact subgroup
                of an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+Lie+group"} exceptional Lie group
                one gets generalized vielbein fields for
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+generalized+geometry"} exceptional generalized geometry
            %li
              %p for the coefficient bundle
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %msub
                                %mi E
                                %mn 8
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi a
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mn 3
                              %mi U
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B} E_8
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathbf{a}}
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)
                      }
              %p
                coming from the second smooth universal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
                one gets part of the geometry of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
          %p
            and so on. More examples are discussed for instance at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+smooth+cohomology+in+string+theory"} twisted smooth cohomology in string theory
          %h3#InTermsOfBasicFormsOnFrameBundle In terms of basic forms on the frame bundle
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = O(n)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            is equivalently an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal
            subbundle of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundle"} frame bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Fr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon Fr(X)\to X
          %p
            This frame bundle carries a universal “basic”
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Fr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau_{b} \in \Omega^1(Fr(X), \mathbb{R}^n)
          %p
            defined on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vector"} tangent vector
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Fr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\in \Gamma_{f \in Fr(X)}
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau_b(v) \coloneqq f^{-1}(d \pi(v))
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mi Fr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\pi \colon T Fr(X)\to T X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            of the bundle projection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is the given frame regarded as a linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi x
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon \mathbb{R}^n \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} T_x X
          %p
            Then given an orthogonal structure in the form of an
            = succeed "-subbundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi Fr
                    %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Fr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon Fr_O(X) \hookrightarrow Fr(X)
            and given finally a local section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fr
                      %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fr_O(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback
            form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi σ
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi b
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau = \sigma^\ast i^\ast \tau_b
                  \\,.
          %p
            (exposition of this in the wider context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrability+of+G-structures"} integrability of G-structures
            includes
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Lott90"} Lott 90, p. 4
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+structure+groups"}> reduction of structure groups
                ,
